  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p43.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For a right triangle, \\[ r=\\frac{a+b-c}{2}. \\] With \\(r=1\\) and \\(c=10,\\) this gives \\(a+b=12.\\) Hence the perimeter is \\[ a+b+c=12+10=22. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "For a right triangle with legs \\(a,b\\) and hypotenuse \\(c,\\) the inradius is \\(\\frac{a+b-c}{2}\\)",
        "Substitute \\(r=1\\) and \\(c=10\\) to find \\(a+b\\)"
      ],
